rings, the Bell of Opening, etc., does little base damage, but does get
the silver damage, though. Silver spellbooks don't. I figure that it'd
just require too much special-casing to make them both silver and paper,
and so paper overrode it so that they'd be vulnerable to fire and so on.

> 	IIRC, wielding a non-weapon item means you do very little damage.
