	If you're trying to keep weaponless, it can definitely be a
useful technique. Hitting things with a wielded non-weapon doesn't break
the conduct. Against silver-haters in general, it may be worth trading
martial arts damage for crappy non-weapon damage plus the rather large
silver bonus, and against shades, it's very much worth it. Better, of
course, is to wear a silver ring and get martial arts damage *and* the
silver bonus, but if you haven't found one, or if silver rings are
something you don't want to be wearing, like hunger or polymorph...

